 "questions": [
  {
   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "L03_001_Print One To N While",
   "display_name": "Print One To N While",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Welcome to Lab 3! So far, every program you've written has done each step exactly once. Now we'll learn <b>loops</b> - a way to repeat a block of code multiple times without writing it out again and again.</p>\n<p>The <code>while</code> loop repeats its indented block <b>as long as</b> a condition stays True. We need a <b>counter</b> variable that we update on every repeat, so that eventually the condition becomes False and the loop stops.</p>\n<pre>i = 1\nwhile i <= 10:\n    print(i)\n    i = i + 1</pre>\n<p>Let's trace through this: <code>i</code> starts at 1. Since <code>1 &lt;= 10</code> is True, we print <code>1</code> and then increase <code>i</code> to 2. We check the condition again: <code>2 &lt;= 10</code> is still True, so we print <code>2</code>, and so on... The loop finally stops once <code>i</code> becomes 11, because <code>11 &lt;= 10</code> is False.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> just like with <code>if</code>, the lines inside the loop body (here, <code>print(i)</code> and <code>i = i + 1</code>) must be indented - press the <b>Tab</b> key once (or 4 spaces) - so Python knows they belong inside the loop. Get this wrong and your loop either won't run correctly or will crash with an <code>IndentationError</code>.</p>\n<p><b>A very common bug:</b> forgetting to update the counter (<code>i = i + 1</code>) inside the loop. If you forget it, <code>i</code> never changes, the condition is always True, and your program runs forever! Always double check your counter update is indented as part of the loop body.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>while</code> loop with a counter starting at 1, print every whole number from 1 to <code>N</code>, each on its own line.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> Input: <pre>4</pre> Output: <pre>1\n2\n3\n4</pre></p>\n<p><b>Example 2 (edge case - N is 1):</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "4",
     "expected": "1\n2\n3\n4",
