  {
   "xml_index": 2,
   "xml_name": "L03_002_Countdown While",
   "display_name": "Countdown While",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Counters don't always have to count upward! Let's make a counter <b>decrease</b> on every repeat instead, to count downward.</p>\n<pre>i = n\nwhile i >= 1:\n    print(i)\n    i = i - 1</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>i</code> starts at <code>n</code> and <b>decreases by 1</b> each time (<code>i = i - 1</code>), and the loop keeps going as long as <code>i</code> is still at least 1.</p>\n<p><b>Trace through:</b> if <code>n = 4</code>: <code>i</code> starts at 4, prints 4, then 3, then 2, then 1 (each time, <code>i &gt;= 1</code> is checked before printing). Once <code>i</code> becomes 0, <code>0 &gt;= 1</code> is False, so the loop stops.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>while</code> loop, print the numbers from <code>N</code> down to 1, each on its own line.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>5</pre> Output: <pre>5\n4\n3\n2\n1</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case:</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
