  {
   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "L03_003_Sum One To N While",
   "display_name": "Sum One To N While",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Loops become really useful when combined with an <b>accumulator</b> variable - a variable that keeps a running total as the loop repeats.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\ntotal = 0\ni = 1\nwhile i <= n:\n    total = total + i\n    i = i + 1\nprint(total)</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>total</code> starts at 0. Every time through the loop, we add the current value of <code>i</code> into <code>total</code>. By the time the loop finishes, <code>total</code> holds the sum of every number the loop visited.</p>\n<p><b>Trace through:</b> if <code>n = 4</code>: <code>total</code> goes 0 -&gt; 1 (add 1) -&gt; 3 (add 2) -&gt; 6 (add 3) -&gt; 10 (add 4). Final answer: <code>10</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>while</code> loop and an accumulator, compute and print the sum of all whole numbers from 1 to <code>N</code> (inclusive).</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>4</pre> Output: <pre>10</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case:</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
