  {
   "xml_index": 4,
   "xml_name": "L03_004_Sum Of Evens While",
   "display_name": "Sum Of Evens While",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's combine what you know about <code>if</code> with a <code>while</code> loop, by putting an <code>if</code> statement <b>inside</b> the loop body. This lets us skip some values while still visiting every number in sequence.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\ntotal = 0\ni = 1\nwhile i <= n:\n    if i % 2 == 0:\n        total = total + i\n    i = i + 1\nprint(total)</pre>\n<p>Notice the loop still checks every number from 1 to <code>n</code>, but <code>total = total + i</code> is now doubly indented - once for being inside the <code>while</code>, and again for being inside the <code>if</code> - so it only runs when <code>i</code> is even.</p>\n<p><b>Trace through:</b> if <code>n = 6</code>: we check 1 (odd, skip), 2 (even, add -&gt; total=2), 3 (skip), 4 (add -&gt; total=6), 5 (skip), 6 (add -&gt; total=12). Final answer: <code>12</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>while</code> loop combined with an <code>if</code>, compute and print the sum of all even numbers from 1 to <code>N</code> (inclusive).</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>6</pre> Output: <pre>12</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (no even numbers at all):</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>0</pre></p>",
