  {
   "xml_index": 7,
   "xml_name": "L03_007_Print One To N For",
   "display_name": "Print One To N For",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <code>while</code> loop needs you to manually create a counter, check it, and update it every time. Python offers a simpler way to repeat something a fixed number of times: the <code>for</code> loop, used together with the <code>range()</code> function.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    print(i)</pre>\n<p><code>range(1, n + 1)</code> produces the sequence of whole numbers starting at 1, up to (but <b>not including</b>) <code>n + 1</code> - in other words, exactly 1, 2, 3, ..., n. The <code>for</code> loop then takes each of these values, one at a time, and puts it into <code>i</code>, running the indented body once per value.</p>\n<p>Notice there's no manual counter to set up or update - <code>i</code> automatically takes each value from the <code>range()</code>, and the loop automatically stops once it runs out of values. This is simpler than <code>while</code>, but only works when you know in advance how many times (or over what sequence) you want to repeat.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> exactly like with <code>while</code>, the body of a <code>for</code> loop must be indented with <b>Tab</b> (or 4 spaces).</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>for</code> loop with <code>range()</code>, print every whole number from 1 to <code>N</code>, each on its own line.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>4</pre> Output: <pre>1\n2\n3\n4</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case:</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "4",
     "expected": "1\n2\n3\n4",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "1",
     "expected": "1",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "5",
     "expected": "1\n2\n3\n4\n5",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
