   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>range()</code> can also take <b>two</b> arguments: <code>range(start, stop)</code>. This produces numbers beginning at <code>start</code>, and stopping just before <code>stop</code> (so <code>stop</code> itself is never included).</p>\n<pre>for i in range(3, 8):\n    print(i)</pre>\n<p>This prints <code>3, 4, 5, 6, 7</code> - it starts at 3, and stops right before 8.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read two whole numbers <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> (one per line), where <code>a</code> is less than <code>b</code>. Using <code>range(a, b + 1)</code>, print every whole number from <code>a</code> to <code>b</code> (inclusive), each on its own line.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>3\n7</pre> Output: <pre>3\n4\n5\n6\n7</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (a and b are the same - just one number):</b> Input: <pre>5\n5</pre> Output: <pre>5</pre></p>",
