   "display_name": "Range With Step Up",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>range()</code> can also take a <b>third</b> argument: the <b>step</b> - how much to add each time, instead of always adding 1.</p>\n<pre>for i in range(0, 10, 2):\n    print(i)</pre>\n<p>This prints <code>0, 2, 4, 6, 8</code> - starting at 0, jumping by 2 each time, and stopping before 10. The step controls the \"jump size\" between consecutive values.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using <code>range()</code> with a step of 2, print every even number from 0 up to (and including, if it fits) <code>N</code>.</p>\n<p>Hint: since <code>range(0, N+1, 2)</code> stops just before <code>N+1</code>, it will correctly include <code>N</code> itself if <code>N</code> is even.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>10</pre> Output: <pre>0\n2\n4\n6\n8\n10</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (N is odd - last even number printed is one less):</b> Input: <pre>7</pre> Output: <pre>0\n2\n4\n6</pre></p>",
