   "xml_name": "L03_011_Range With Step Down",
   "display_name": "Range With Step Down",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A step can also be <b>negative</b>! This makes <code>range()</code> count <b>downward</b> instead of upward.</p>\n<pre>for i in range(10, 0, -1):\n    print(i)</pre>\n<p>This prints <code>10, 9, 8, ..., 1</code> - starting at 10, subtracting 1 each time (because the step is <code>-1</code>), and stopping just before 0 (so 0 itself is not printed).</p>\n<p><b>Important:</b> when counting down, <code>stop</code> must be <b>less</b> than <code>start</code>, and the step must be negative - otherwise <code>range()</code> produces no values at all!</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using <code>range()</code> with a step of <code>-1</code>, print every whole number from <code>N</code> down to 1 (inclusive).</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>5</pre> Output: <pre>5\n4\n3\n2\n1</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case:</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
