  {
   "xml_index": 13,
   "xml_name": "L03_013_Sum One To N For",
   "display_name": "Sum One To N For",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Just like with <code>while</code>, we can use an accumulator inside a <code>for</code> loop to build up a running total.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\ntotal = 0\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    total = total + i\nprint(total)</pre>\n<p>This works exactly the same way as the <code>while</code> version you wrote earlier - <code>total</code> starts at 0, and each pass through the loop adds the current value of <code>i</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>for</code> loop and an accumulator, compute and print the sum of all whole numbers from 1 to <code>N</code> (inclusive).</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>4</pre> Output: <pre>10</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case:</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
