   "xml_name": "L03_014_Print Evens For",
   "display_name": "Print Evens For",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's combine an <code>if</code> inside a <code>for</code> loop, the same way you did with <code>while</code> earlier.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    if i % 2 == 0:\n        print(i)</pre>\n<p>The loop still visits every number from 1 to <code>n</code>, but the <code>print(i)</code> only runs when <code>i</code> is even, thanks to the nested <code>if</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>for</code> loop combined with an <code>if</code>, print all even numbers from 1 to <code>N</code> (inclusive), each on its own line.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>8</pre> Output: <pre>2\n4\n6\n8</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (no even numbers):</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <i>(nothing printed)</i></p>",
