   "xml_name": "L03_015_Count Multiples Of K",
   "display_name": "Count Multiples Of K",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's use a <code>for</code> loop with a counter variable (separate from the loop's own <code>i</code>) to count how many numbers satisfy a condition, rather than printing them.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\nk = int(input())\ncount = 0\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    if i % k == 0:\n        count = count + 1\nprint(count)</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>count</code> is an accumulator too, just like <code>total</code> in earlier questions - except instead of adding <code>i</code> itself, we add exactly <code>1</code> every time the condition is True, effectively counting how many times it happened.</p>\n<p><b>Trace through:</b> if <code>n = 10, k = 3</code>: multiples of 3 up to 10 are 3, 6, 9 - that's 3 of them, so <code>count</code> ends at <code>3</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read two whole numbers <code>N</code> and <code>K</code> (one per line). Count and print how many numbers from 1 to <code>N</code> (inclusive) are multiples of <code>K</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>10\n3</pre> Output: <pre>3</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (no multiples in range):</b> Input: <pre>2\n5</pre> Output: <pre>0</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
