   "xml_name": "L03_017_Average Of N Numbers",
   "display_name": "Average Of N Numbers",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's use a <code>for</code> loop to read <b>several</b> numbers, one per line, and compute their average - a very common real-world pattern where the amount of input depends on a count given up front.</p>\n<p><b>Reminder:</b> since we're computing a float result, round it using <code>round(value, 2)</code> before printing, to avoid tiny floating-point mismatches.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\ntotal = 0\nfor i in range(n):\n    x = int(input())\n    total = total + x\naverage = total / n\nprint(round(average, 2))</pre>\n<p>Here, each pass through the loop reads <b>one more number</b> using <code>input()</code>, and immediately adds it to the running total - we don't need to store all the numbers, just their sum.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>, then read <code>N</code> more whole numbers (one per line). Print their average, rounded to 2 decimal places.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>3\n10\n20\n30</pre> Output: <pre>20.0</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (only one number - average is itself):</b> Input: <pre>1\n7</pre> Output: <pre>7.0</pre></p>",
