   "display_name": "Vertically Flipped Triangle",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Now let's flip the original right-angle triangle <b>vertically</b> (upside down) - the widest row comes first, and each row after that has one fewer star.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\nfor row in range(n, 0, -1):\n    for col in range(row):\n        print(\"*\", end=\"\")\n    print()</pre>\n<p>The only change from the original triangle is that the <b>outer</b> loop now counts <b>down</b> from <code>n</code> to 1 (using a step of <code>-1</code>), instead of up from 1 to <code>n</code>. The inner loop logic (printing <code>row</code> stars) stays exactly the same.</p>\n<p><b>Trace through (n=3):</b> Row (outer value) 3: 3 stars -&gt; <code>***</code>. Row 2: 2 stars -&gt; <code>**</code>. Row 1: 1 star -&gt; <code>*</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>n</code> (between 1 and 5). Print an upside-down right-angle triangle of stars with <code>n</code> rows, starting with <code>n</code> stars and ending with 1 star.</p>\n<p><b>Example (n=3):</b> Output: <pre>***\n**\n*</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (n=1):</b> Output: <pre>*</pre></p>",
