   "xml_name": "L03_023_Equilateral Pyramid",
   "display_name": "Equilateral Pyramid",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's build a centered pyramid shape, where each row is padded with spaces on the left so the stars line up symmetrically, like a triangle with all sides equal.</p>\n<p>For a pyramid of <code>n</code> rows, row <code>r</code> (counting from 1) needs <code>n - r</code> spaces, followed by <code>2*r - 1</code> stars.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\nfor row in range(1, n + 1):\n    for space in range(n - row):\n        print(\" \", end=\"\")\n    for col in range(2 * row - 1):\n        print(\"*\", end=\"\")\n    print()</pre>\n<p><b>Trace through (n=3):</b> Row 1: <code>3-1=2</code> spaces, <code>2*1-1=1</code> star -&gt; <code>\"  *\"</code>. Row 2: <code>3-2=1</code> space, <code>2*2-1=3</code> stars -&gt; <code>\" ***\"</code>. Row 3: <code>3-3=0</code> spaces, <code>2*3-1=5</code> stars -&gt; <code>\"*****\"</code>. The result is a symmetric pyramid, one star wider on each side per row.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>n</code> (between 1 and 5). Print a centered pyramid of stars with <code>n</code> rows, as described above.</p>\n<p><b>Example (n=3):</b> Output: <pre>  *\n ***\n*****</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (n=1):</b> Output: <pre>*</pre></p>",
