   "display_name": "Digit Repeat Rows",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Nested loops don't have to print stars - let's print a number pattern instead, where row <code>r</code> shows the digit <code>r</code> repeated <code>r</code> times.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\nfor row in range(1, n + 1):\n    for col in range(row):\n        print(row, end=\"\")\n    print()</pre>\n<p>The only change from the original right-angle triangle: instead of always printing <code>\"*\"</code>, we print <code>row</code> itself (converted to text automatically by <code>print</code>) each time through the inner loop.</p>\n<p><b>Trace through (n=3):</b> Row 1: print <code>1</code> once -&gt; <code>\"1\"</code>. Row 2: print <code>2</code> twice -&gt; <code>\"22\"</code>. Row 3: print <code>3</code> three times -&gt; <code>\"333\"</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>n</code> (between 1 and 5). Print <code>n</code> rows where row <code>r</code> contains the digit <code>r</code> repeated <code>r</code> times.</p>\n<p><b>Example (n=3):</b> Output: <pre>1\n22\n333</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (n=1):</b> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
