   "xml_name": "L03_026_Growing Number Triangle",
   "display_name": "Growing Number Triangle",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's try one more number pattern: row <code>r</code> shows the digits 1 through <code>r</code> written next to each other (not repeated - counting up each time).</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\nfor row in range(1, n + 1):\n    for col in range(1, row + 1):\n        print(col, end=\"\")\n    print()</pre>\n<p>Here the <b>inner</b> loop variable <code>col</code> itself counts from 1 up to <code>row</code>, and we print <code>col</code> at each step - so row 3 prints <code>1</code>, then <code>2</code>, then <code>3</code>, giving <code>\"123\"</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Trace through (n=3):</b> Row 1: just <code>1</code> -&gt; <code>\"1\"</code>. Row 2: <code>1</code> then <code>2</code> -&gt; <code>\"12\"</code>. Row 3: <code>1</code>, <code>2</code>, <code>3</code> -&gt; <code>\"123\"</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>n</code> (between 1 and 5). Print <code>n</code> rows where row <code>r</code> contains the digits 1 through <code>r</code> written next to each other, with no spaces.</p>\n<p><b>Example (n=3):</b> Output: <pre>1\n12\n123</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (n=1):</b> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
