  {
   "xml_index": 27,
   "xml_name": "L03_027_Multiplication Grid",
   "display_name": "Multiplication Grid",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's use a nested loop to print a full multiplication grid, rather than just a single number's table - every row is a different number's table, giving a proper 2D grid of results.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\nfor row in range(1, n + 1):\n    for col in range(1, n + 1):\n        print(row * col, end=\" \")\n    print()</pre>\n<p>The <b>outer</b> loop picks which row (multiplier) we're on; the <b>inner</b> loop goes across that row, computing <code>row * col</code> for each column. We use <code>end=\" \"</code> this time (a space, not nothing) so consecutive numbers on a row don't run together.</p>\n<p><b>Trace through (n=3):</b> Row 1: <code>1*1=1</code>, <code>1*2=2</code>, <code>1*3=3</code> -&gt; <code>\"1 2 3 \"</code>. Row 2: <code>2*1=2</code>, <code>2*2=4</code>, <code>2*3=6</code> -&gt; <code>\"2 4 6 \"</code>. Row 3: <code>3 6 9</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>n</code> (between 1 and 5). Print an <code>n</code> by <code>n</code> multiplication grid, where the entry in row <code>r</code>, column <code>c</code> is <code>r * c</code>, with a space after each number (including the last one on each row), and each row on its own line.</p>\n<p><b>Example (n=3):</b> Output: <pre>1 2 3 \n2 4 6 \n3 6 9 </pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (n=1):</b> Output: <pre>1 </pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
