  {
   "xml_index": 32,
   "xml_name": "L03_032_Sum Of Two Indexed Elements",
   "display_name": "Sum Of Two Indexed Elements",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>You can index the same list more than once and combine the results with ordinary arithmetic, just like any other variable.</p>\n<pre>Lst = [5, 10, 15, 20, 25]\na = int(input())\nb = int(input())\nprint(Lst[a] + Lst[b])</pre>\n<p><b>Trace through:</b> if the user enters <code>1</code> then <code>3</code>, we compute <code>Lst[1] + Lst[3]</code>, which is <code>10 + 20 = 30</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Using the fixed list <code>Lst = [5, 10, 15, 20, 25]</code>, read two whole number indices <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> (each between 0 and 4, one per line) and print the sum of the elements at those two positions.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> Input: <pre>1\n3</pre> Output: <pre>30</pre></p>\n<p><b>Example 2 (edge case - same index twice):</b> Input: <pre>0\n0</pre> Output: <pre>10</pre></p>",
