  {
   "xml_index": 35,
   "xml_name": "L03_035_Sum Of Elements Greater Than X",
   "display_name": "Sum Of Elements Greater Than X",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's combine iterating over a list with an accumulator, just like you did with ranges of numbers earlier.</p>\n<pre>Lst = [3, 12, 7, 20, 5, 16]\nx = int(input())\ntotal = 0\nfor value in Lst:\n    if value > x:\n        total = total + value\nprint(total)</pre>\n<p>This works exactly like the \"sum of evens\" pattern from before, except now we're looping over the list's actual elements (using <code>for value in Lst</code>) instead of a range of numbers.</p>\n<p><b>Trace through:</b> if <code>x = 10</code>: elements greater than 10 are 12, 20, 16. Sum: <code>12 + 20 + 16 = 48</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Using the fixed list <code>Lst = [3, 12, 7, 20, 5, 16]</code>, read a whole number <code>x</code> and print the sum of all elements greater than <code>x</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>10</pre> Output: <pre>48</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (nothing qualifies - sum is 0):</b> Input: <pre>100</pre> Output: <pre>0</pre></p>",
