   "xml_name": "L03_036_Sum Of List Using While And Len",
   "display_name": "Sum Of List Using While And Len",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's compute the sum of an <strong>entire</strong> list using a <code>while</code> loop with an explicit index and the <code>len()</code> function you just saw - this is the classic pattern for \"process every element of a list\" when you specifically need to track positions.</p>\n<pre>Lst = [8, 3, 15, 6, 12, 9, 4]\ntotal = 0\ni = 0\nwhile i &lt; len(Lst):\n    total = total + Lst[i]\n    i = i + 1\nprint(total)</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>i</code> starts at 0 (the first valid index) and the loop continues as long as <code>i</code> is a valid index, i.e. less than <code>len(Lst)</code>. Each pass adds <code>Lst[i]</code> into the total, then moves to the next index.</p>\n<p><strong>Your task:</strong> Using the fixed list <code>Lst = [8, 3, 15, 6, 12, 9, 4]</code>, compute and print the sum of all its elements using a <code>while</code> loop and <code>len()</code>, exactly as shown above.</p>\n<p><strong>Example:</strong> Output:</p>\n<pre>57</pre>\n<p></p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Do not change this list\nLst = [8, 3, 15, 6, 12, 9, 4]\n# write your code here to find the sum using a while loop:",
