   "display_name": "Count Occurrences Of Value",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Lists can contain <b>repeated</b> values. Let's count how many times a particular value appears, using a loop and a counter (the <code>in</code> operator alone can only tell us whether a value appears - not how many times).</p>\n<pre>Lst = [4, 7, 4, 2, 4, 9, 7]\nx = int(input())\ncount = 0\nfor value in Lst:\n    if value == x:\n        count = count + 1\nprint(count)</pre>\n<p><b>Trace through:</b> if <code>x = 4</code>: we scan the list and find <code>4</code> at three positions. So <code>count</code> ends at <code>3</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Using the fixed list <code>Lst = [4, 7, 4, 2, 4, 9, 7]</code>, read a whole number <code>x</code> and print how many times it appears in the list.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> Input: <pre>4</pre> Output: <pre>3</pre></p>\n<p><b>Example 2 (edge case - value not in list at all):</b> Input: <pre>100</pre> Output: <pre>0</pre></p>",
